WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:02.770
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:03.970 --> 00:05.850
Good morning, Boxxo!

00:05.850 --> 00:06.870
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:06.870 --> 00:08.850
Good morning, Lammis!

00:09.270 --> 00:12.850
Karios, Gorth! Thanks for 
keeping watch again today!

00:12.850 --> 00:16.110
Sure. Nothing beats sweet tea 
at the end of a night shift.

00:16.980 --> 00:19.420
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>

00:18.170 --> 00:19.420
Mhm!

00:20.710 --> 00:23.450
<i>I died and was reborn as a vending machine.</i>

00:23.450 --> 00:26.320
<i>That's a bizarre situation 
to suddenly be in...</i>

00:26.320 --> 00:27.500
Good morning!

00:27.500 --> 00:30.740
<i>but I've found ways to make 
the whole thing enjoyable.</i>

00:34.170 --> 00:37.010
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:39.470 --> 00:41.060
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

00:41.320 --> 00:43.300
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

00:43.300 --> 00:48.720
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

00:44.390 --> 00:50.270
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:48.720 --> 00:51.140
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

00:51.140 --> 00:52.870
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:07.060 --> 02:10.980
<b>Hunters and Motives</b>

02:09.440 --> 02:11.380
It really feels like summer now!

02:11.380 --> 02:12.600
<i>Hello there.</i>

02:12.600 --> 02:14.730
Yeah, how time flies.

02:14.950 --> 02:19.740
<i>Oh yeah. It's easy to forget when 
there's a sky and changing seasons,</i>

02:19.740 --> 02:23.110
<i>but we're inside a dungeon 
with multiple strata.</i>

02:23.530 --> 02:27.180
<i>Once it gets hotter,
I'll start selling ice cream.</i>

02:23.660 --> 02:27.750
<b>Excellent Hyper Ice Cream</b>

02:26.670 --> 02:27.870
Boxxo.

02:27.870 --> 02:29.380
<i>Oh hey, Mishuel.</i>

02:29.380 --> 02:31.640
I have a major request for you.

02:31.640 --> 02:33.630
<i>Why the serious, formal look?</i>

02:33.630 --> 02:36.880
You see, I've been pondering 
an idea for a while now.

02:36.880 --> 02:37.880
Boxxo!

02:37.880 --> 02:40.260
Despite your steel body, 
you are noble and kind.

02:40.260 --> 02:43.010
Your defense is top notch,
and you can even revive the dead.

02:43.010 --> 02:45.430
It makes no difference 
if you're a magic item!

02:45.430 --> 02:46.990
I'm enamored with you!

02:47.270 --> 02:47.900
<i>What?</i>

02:47.900 --> 02:49.150
<i>E-Enamored?</i>

02:49.150 --> 02:53.220
Boxxo! May I call you "master" as of today?!

02:53.220 --> 02:56.450
<i>By "enamored with," you 
mean platonically, right?</i>

02:56.890 --> 02:58.280
Is your answer "no"?!

02:58.280 --> 03:02.040
<i>Mishuel is a master hunter,
but his social skills are abysmal.</i>

03:02.400 --> 03:05.310
<i>I'm sure it took a lot of courage 
for him to say all that.</i>

03:05.310 --> 03:07.260
<i>I'll be mature about this.</i>

03:07.260 --> 03:08.650
<i>Hello there.</i>

03:09.250 --> 03:10.930
That means you accept!

03:10.930 --> 03:13.290
Thank you, Master Boxxo!

03:13.290 --> 03:17.540
<i>Th-This hug is just a hug, r-right?</i>

03:19.650 --> 03:22.820
Somebody's got themselves an apprentice.

03:21.800 --> 03:23.930
I'm impressed, Boxxo.

03:23.440 --> 03:27.670
<i>Wh-Whoa! Apprentice or not, 
I've got nothing to teach him!</i>

03:28.010 --> 03:29.440
All right, Master Boxxo.

03:29.440 --> 03:31.590
The first thing I'll do is wipe you down.

03:31.590 --> 03:33.100
C'mon, Mishuel!

03:33.100 --> 03:36.160
I'm the one who wipes him down! 
You don't need to bother!

03:36.160 --> 03:37.470
Oh, I see.

03:37.470 --> 03:40.690
I apologize for being so intrusive.

03:40.690 --> 03:43.780
Excellent, you're all here.

03:43.780 --> 03:45.210
Director Bear.

03:45.210 --> 03:48.150
Boxxo, Lammis, Hulemy, Mishuel.

03:48.150 --> 03:51.870
We're about to hold an important 
meeting at the Dead's Lament's stratum.

03:51.870 --> 03:53.910
I'd love for you to accompany me.

03:53.920 --> 03:56.920
<b>The Dead's Lament Stratum</b>

04:03.410 --> 04:06.020
These, along with the magic item Boxxo,

04:06.020 --> 04:09.420
are the survivors of an encounter 
with the Netherlord.

04:09.420 --> 04:14.690
So, that item is the much-talked-about 
box that sells unusual objects.

04:14.690 --> 04:18.150
<b>Director Origin</b>

04:14.690 --> 04:18.150
<b>Dog Mountain Director</b>

04:14.690 --> 04:19.900
He also has other useful abilities that 
have saved us on many an occasion.

04:19.900 --> 04:20.850
Oh yeah?

04:21.200 --> 04:24.920
<i>It </i>is<i> an important meeting, 
if the directors of each stratum's</i>

04:24.920 --> 04:27.100
<i>Hunters Association are here.</i>

04:25.160 --> 04:28.410
<b>Director Scorching</b>

04:27.100 --> 04:29.120
Let's get right to the point.

04:29.120 --> 04:34.870
The Netherlord who appeared a few days ago 
is no doubt the Demon Lord's left-arm general.

04:35.690 --> 04:37.250
That means trouble.

04:37.250 --> 04:39.070
<i>The Netherlord.</i>

04:39.070 --> 04:42.610
<i>The mysterious four-armed 
skeleton that suddenly appeared</i>

04:42.610 --> 04:45.710
<i>when we defeated the Dead's 
Lament stratum lord.</i>

04:46.110 --> 04:49.350
<i>He stopped Hulemy's and 
Shui's hearts using magic,</i>

04:49.350 --> 04:54.390
<i>but I turned into an AED, and my 
electroshocks successfully resuscitated them.</i>

04:55.610 --> 05:00.670
<i>It's a relief that nobody died, but we 
can't let a dude like him run free.</i>

05:01.530 --> 05:05.800
<i>That's Kerioyl, leader of 
the Menagerie of Fools.</i>

05:05.800 --> 05:08.060
<i>I can't see his face, but he seems 
way more menacing than usual.</i>

05:08.540 --> 05:11.920
Excuse me. What is a left-arm general?

05:11.920 --> 05:17.520
Outside this dungeon, far to the north, 
is a land ruled by the Demon Lord.

05:17.520 --> 05:19.090
<i>There's a Demon Lord?!</i>

05:19.090 --> 05:22.920
<i>Well, maybe it'd be unnatural in a 
world like this if there weren't one.</i>

05:22.920 --> 05:26.740
If you regard the Demon 
Lord himself as the head,

05:26.740 --> 05:31.250
the others are ranked in descending order: 
Right arm, left arm, right leg, and left leg.

05:31.250 --> 05:35.900
In other words, the left-arm general 
is number three in the Demon Lord's forces.

05:35.900 --> 05:37.610
Number three...

05:38.020 --> 05:40.890
What was a leader of the Demon Lord's 
forces doing in a place like that?

05:40.890 --> 05:43.530
Demon Lord's forces? That's bad news.

05:43.530 --> 05:49.030
They would have to get past fortified cities 
and empires to invade us, which seems unlikely.

05:49.030 --> 05:50.910
So, what do we do?

05:50.910 --> 05:55.320
He attacked association members inside 
the dungeon, on our collective watch.

05:55.320 --> 05:59.030
We hit him with everything 
we've got, of course!

05:59.030 --> 06:01.640
You don't get this fired up very often.

06:01.640 --> 06:04.380
Letting him get away with that 
stunt would be bad for business.

06:04.380 --> 06:06.930
We've got some skilled 
hunters who'll take part!

06:07.210 --> 06:09.430
The Origin stratum will provide some, too.

06:09.430 --> 06:13.060
After what he put my people through,
it's payback time.

06:13.390 --> 06:15.580
I shall take part as well.

06:15.580 --> 06:17.560
I, too, wish to settle the score!

06:17.560 --> 06:19.320
Count me in, too.

06:19.320 --> 06:23.950
After what happened to Hulemy and Shui, 
I won't be happy until I sock him one!

06:23.950 --> 06:25.370
Right, Boxxo?

06:25.370 --> 06:26.820
<i>Hello there.</i>

06:27.290 --> 06:30.450
Hulemy, you can help us by planning things.

06:30.700 --> 06:34.020
Get real. That guy tried to kill me.

06:34.020 --> 06:36.080
I'll pay him back firsthand.

06:36.350 --> 06:38.830
Hulemy! Yeah!

06:38.830 --> 06:42.080
I can see how enthusiastic you are.

06:42.080 --> 06:45.600
Clearflow Lake will put 
its top people on this.

06:45.600 --> 06:49.740
Let's all work together to 
bring down the Netherlord!

06:49.740 --> 06:51.130
Yeah!

06:51.600 --> 06:55.810
<i>This is when I can't help but 
think, "If I only had arms."</i>

06:57.100 --> 07:01.500
<i>It wasn't long before the aces 
showed up from each stratum.</i>

07:04.430 --> 07:07.090
Hi, Lammis, Hulemy, Boxxo.

07:07.650 --> 07:09.460
You two are in the assault squad, too?

07:09.460 --> 07:10.650
You bet!

07:11.440 --> 07:13.660
Hello, Boxxo.

07:13.660 --> 07:16.830
I'd been wondering where 
you'd gotten off to.

07:16.830 --> 07:19.860
Let's see, think I'll buy 
the usual water and soup.

07:19.860 --> 07:22.850
Today's the day I get 
lucky with those numbers.

07:22.850 --> 07:26.000
<i>Huh? The gate guards are one thing,</i>

07:26.000 --> 07:29.170
<i>but why are the elderly couple I see 
every morning in the assault squad?</i>

07:29.170 --> 07:31.300
<b>Unable to dispense prize</b>

07:29.170 --> 07:31.300
<b>Out of change</b>

07:29.170 --> 07:31.300
<b>Vending</b>

07:29.170 --> 07:31.300
<b>Yen</b>

07:31.690 --> 07:33.800
Boxxo, Lammis.

07:33.800 --> 07:35.390
The school director!

07:35.870 --> 07:39.340
I heard you were there when 
Shui needed you. Thanks.

07:39.340 --> 07:42.440
<i>She runs an orphanage in the Origin stratum.</i>

07:42.440 --> 07:45.370
<i>I'm pretty sure she taught 
Shui archery, too.</i>

07:45.730 --> 07:48.960
Oh hey, Hoxie. You're coming along, too?

07:48.960 --> 07:50.790
Have you been well?

07:50.790 --> 07:53.740
Yes to both questions, Shimelai, Yumite.

07:54.110 --> 07:56.380
<i>These three all know each other?!</i>

07:56.380 --> 07:58.990
<i>Does that mean the couple 
are amazing hunters, too?!</i>

07:59.650 --> 08:04.290
<i>That day, ace hunters came 
rushing here from each stratum,</i>

08:04.290 --> 08:07.490
<i>and we held a kickoff party prior 
to going after the Netherlord.</i>

08:07.880 --> 08:09.950
So many different types of people!

08:09.950 --> 08:14.010
Chances are, each of them possess 
some powerful blessing.

08:14.260 --> 08:17.020
What's with all the old folks?

08:17.020 --> 08:20.270
This is no nursing home. 
Are you up for this?

08:20.270 --> 08:24.890
Hey, you should mind your manners 
if you know what's good for you.

08:24.890 --> 08:28.560
Come again? You tryin' to 
start something with me?

08:28.560 --> 08:29.580
You know who we are?!

08:29.580 --> 08:30.240
<i>Oh.</i>

08:30.240 --> 08:31.660
<i>Hello there.</i>

08:31.660 --> 08:33.540
What's up? A quarrel?

08:33.540 --> 08:36.650
Hey Lammis, poke him a 
little and knock him out.

08:36.650 --> 08:39.740
What, are you with these guys?

08:39.740 --> 08:41.540
Yeah, I sure am.

08:41.540 --> 08:45.210
But technically, I'm still trying 
to get them to join my group.

08:45.210 --> 08:46.910
Captain Kerioyl.

08:47.910 --> 08:49.610
K-Kerioyl?

08:49.610 --> 08:53.540
You don't mean Captain Kerioyl 
of the Menagerie of Fools?

08:53.540 --> 08:55.090
And what'll you do if that's me?

08:56.950 --> 09:00.560
N-Nothing at all, sir!

09:02.010 --> 09:06.220
I am Kerioyl, leader of 
the Menagerie of Fools.

09:06.220 --> 09:10.300
Especially as my members are out of 
commission, I'm grateful for your help.

09:10.560 --> 09:14.430
<i>Oh! It's rare for the captain 
to greet anyone so politely!</i>

09:14.870 --> 09:18.370
<i>By the way, Shui and the red/white 
twins have yet to recover,</i>

09:18.370 --> 09:20.190
<i>so they're apparently sitting this one out.</i>

09:20.190 --> 09:22.700
<i>Not that they wanted to stay behind.</i>

09:23.700 --> 09:25.630
My name is Mishuel!

09:25.630 --> 09:30.080
I am young and inexperienced, but I look 
forward to your guidance and encouragement!

09:30.080 --> 09:33.370
I am Hoxie, from the Origin stratum.

09:33.370 --> 09:35.060
I am Yumite.

09:35.060 --> 09:38.980
My blessings are a bit of healing light,
a bit of swordsmanship.

09:39.850 --> 09:41.750
I am Shimelai.

09:41.750 --> 09:44.720
I know magic, and possess several blessings.

09:44.720 --> 09:46.850
Once again, I am Karios.

09:46.850 --> 09:48.230
I am Gorth.

09:48.510 --> 09:52.640
I'm Hulemy, a magic item engineer 
and Lammis' childhood friend.

09:52.640 --> 09:54.200
I'm Lammis.

09:54.200 --> 09:56.640
And this is my partner, Boxxo.

09:56.640 --> 09:58.230
<i>Hello there.</i>

09:59.490 --> 10:02.740
<i>A vanguard, rear guard, and recovery team.</i>

10:02.740 --> 10:05.070
<i>That's a fairly well-balanced party.</i>

10:05.070 --> 10:08.120
<i>Although our older members' strength 
has yet to be demonstrated.</i>

10:08.120 --> 10:12.370
<i>I'm sure Captain Kerioyl 
will make good calls.</i>

10:12.370 --> 10:15.250
We start searching for him tomorrow.

10:15.250 --> 10:18.000
Let's get revenge on that bonehead!

10:18.000 --> 10:20.030
Yeah!

10:23.450 --> 10:24.230
Boxxo.

10:24.230 --> 10:24.930
Boxxo.

10:24.930 --> 10:26.160
Boxxo.

10:24.930 --> 10:27.020
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

10:28.520 --> 10:31.980
<b>The Dead's Lament Stratum</b>

10:28.790 --> 10:31.390
<i>The following day,
we split into several teams,</i>

10:31.390 --> 10:34.520
<i>and each headed toward its search target.</i>

10:34.520 --> 10:37.910
I'm sorry to saddle you all 
with this dangerous task.

10:37.910 --> 10:43.480
You never change. Still so 
formal after all this time.

10:43.480 --> 10:48.060
That's right. We're all comrades, 
so no need to apologize.

10:49.410 --> 10:51.880
There's a sight that brings back memories.

10:52.800 --> 10:56.240
Everyone, there are monsters 
lying in wait up ahead.

10:56.720 --> 10:59.920
Why don't Yumite, Hoxie, 
and I deal with them?

10:59.920 --> 11:04.050
Another group effort with my 
senior members? Sounds exciting.

11:04.050 --> 11:06.310
O light, enshroud my arrowheads.

11:09.800 --> 11:11.930
Ah, three at once.

11:11.930 --> 11:13.290
Well done.

11:13.290 --> 11:16.190
She fights as dirty as ever.

11:16.190 --> 11:18.190
Oh, really?

11:18.500 --> 11:22.920
Looks like they're so far away,
the monsters still haven't noticed us.

11:23.340 --> 11:25.020
Then I'll give them an invite!

11:40.210 --> 11:43.950
Good show, you three. Looks like 
your skills haven't declined.

11:43.950 --> 11:46.980
Nah, we're not in top form anymore.

11:46.980 --> 11:50.320
I'd better polish up my magic.

11:50.320 --> 11:52.860
My cuts aren't as sharp as they were.

11:53.680 --> 11:56.180
If only we didn't have to age.

11:56.180 --> 11:59.430
I could never brag about this to Shui.

11:59.430 --> 12:01.100
I'd best give it some thought.

12:01.100 --> 12:02.680
Talk about impressive!

12:02.680 --> 12:04.990
Boxxo, we'd better work to keep up.

12:05.190 --> 12:06.610
<i>Hello there.</i>

12:11.000 --> 12:13.620
This tastes so good!

12:13.620 --> 12:15.970
I bet Shui would be jealous.

12:15.970 --> 12:19.490
I'd like to try every one of 
his foods on this campaign.

12:19.490 --> 12:24.160
Just being able to eat Boxxo's food 
every meal is enough to motivate me!

12:24.160 --> 12:26.330
Yeah, you said it.

12:26.330 --> 12:30.130
<i>Come back for as many helpings as 
you want, if it'll up your morale.</i>

12:34.710 --> 12:38.030
Lammis, lower your center of gravity.

12:38.280 --> 12:42.280
That'll make things easier, and 
improve your power and accuracy.

12:42.280 --> 12:43.590
My center of gravity?

12:44.030 --> 12:45.420
All right.

12:49.940 --> 12:51.550
That felt great!

12:51.550 --> 12:53.320
And it looked great.

12:53.320 --> 12:57.360
You should get used to how it feels 
to fight when Boxxo isn't present.

12:58.220 --> 12:59.140
I will!

13:00.600 --> 13:04.180
<i>Blessing of Might gives Lammis more 
strength than she can handle.</i>

13:04.180 --> 13:06.410
<i>It requires effort to control herself.</i>

13:06.790 --> 13:10.180
<i>Usually she has me on her back, which 
provides just the right handicap.</i>

13:10.180 --> 13:13.220
<i>If she could draw out her strength 
well enough without me...</i>

13:17.160 --> 13:18.850
<i>You can do it, Lammis!</i>

13:28.020 --> 13:30.630
Hey, Boxxo. You got a minute?

13:30.630 --> 13:32.070
<i>Hello there.</i>

13:32.500 --> 13:34.450
Something doesn't make sense to me.

13:34.860 --> 13:39.160
It sounds like the Netherlord 
let Lammis go on purpose.

13:39.160 --> 13:40.380
<i>Hulemy...</i>

13:41.130 --> 13:46.180
If we'd been wiped out then, 
we'd never have reported back.

13:46.180 --> 13:49.840
This assault force probably still 
wouldn't have been put together.

13:50.070 --> 13:54.270
In other words, what if his 
goal is to use himself as bait

13:54.270 --> 13:56.710
to gather ace hunters here to this stratum?

13:57.950 --> 14:01.600
<i>If you're right about that, 
we really fell for it.</i>

14:03.730 --> 14:05.150
Hup.

14:05.610 --> 14:08.240
But I don't know what happens after that.

14:08.240 --> 14:10.250
There's always the worst-case scenario,

14:10.250 --> 14:13.710
but I'm not about to confuse everyone 
by telling them my speculation.

14:13.710 --> 14:15.630
You're the only one I can tell, Boxxo.

14:16.030 --> 14:17.500
<i>Hello there.</i>

14:18.180 --> 14:20.620
Thanks, don't mind if I do.

14:22.120 --> 14:25.730
<i>Why not have some warm milk tea, and relax?</i>

14:28.160 --> 14:31.140
The flow of magic power seems odd.

14:31.140 --> 14:34.110
It's increasing, and growing unsettled.

14:34.110 --> 14:36.510
This could mean trouble.

14:37.080 --> 14:39.350
<i>The old guy was right.</i>

14:39.350 --> 14:44.370
<i>Not long afterward, we learned that another 
hunter team had found the Netherlord.</i>

15:14.550 --> 15:17.050
Good, we got around behind him.

15:17.050 --> 15:20.080
Hoxie and Shimelai will provide 
covering fire from here.

15:20.080 --> 15:21.310
Understood.

15:21.310 --> 15:23.930
Karios and Gorth, you'll stand guard.

15:23.930 --> 15:24.730
Sure!

15:23.930 --> 15:25.290
By your order.

15:25.560 --> 15:29.430
Lammis, we have tons of aces.
No need to go nuts.

15:29.430 --> 15:31.060
Yeah, I'll do my best!

15:31.060 --> 15:32.770
We're counting on you too, Boxxo.

15:32.770 --> 15:34.320
<i>Hello there.</i>

15:34.320 --> 15:36.280
Everyone else will charge.

15:36.280 --> 15:40.290
Our goal is to slay the Netherlord, 
but don't do anything reckless.

15:40.290 --> 15:42.580
If we buy time, reinforcements will arrive.

15:42.580 --> 15:43.250
Yes, sir!

15:42.580 --> 15:43.250
Yes.

15:42.580 --> 15:43.250
Yeah.

15:42.580 --> 15:43.830
Count on me!

15:43.830 --> 15:46.680
Let's show him what we can do!

16:08.430 --> 16:10.790
<i>Form change!</i>

16:11.440 --> 16:13.690
<i>Power washer!</i>

16:11.450 --> 16:12.400
<b>Refreshing
 Mr. Pressure</b>

16:11.450 --> 16:12.400
<b>Coin-Op
 Power
 Washer</b>

16:11.450 --> 16:12.400
<b>Osugi Cleaning Factory</b>

16:13.690 --> 16:17.960
<i>And with Telekinesis—the new blessing 
I got in that last battle—</i>

16:17.960 --> 16:22.450
<i>I've been training every night to build 
up my physical strength and dexterity!</i>

16:22.450 --> 16:24.840
<i>Now I can even do something like this!</i>

16:25.290 --> 16:28.210
<i>I'm really not a vending machine anymore.</i>

16:28.210 --> 16:29.670
<i>But what else is new?</i>

16:30.210 --> 16:32.040
Wow, Boxxo!

16:32.040 --> 16:33.590
<i>You win!</i>

16:50.510 --> 16:54.150
Looks like we won't get anywhere 
until we defeat the Netherlord.

16:54.150 --> 16:58.270
Yes, he appears to be 
using some sort of spell.

17:02.290 --> 17:04.790
Everyone get away from there!

17:04.790 --> 17:08.030
A vast amount of magic power is 
gathering to the Netherlord!

17:08.030 --> 17:11.290
It's probably some big explosion spell!

17:11.590 --> 17:12.210
Let's split!

17:12.210 --> 17:13.040
Right!

17:13.040 --> 17:14.930
But the other hunters!

17:15.130 --> 17:16.460
I'm on it!

17:17.920 --> 17:19.900
I suggest you cover your ears!

17:20.430 --> 17:22.790
<i>But I don't have any hands!</i>

17:22.790 --> 17:25.320
<i>Or ears, or eardrums...</i>

17:25.320 --> 17:28.600
Major spell incoming! Fall back!

17:29.550 --> 17:31.800
Why go and do that?

17:31.800 --> 17:33.820
But was it in time?

17:38.570 --> 17:40.150
<i>Deploying barrier!</i>

17:58.670 --> 18:00.690
Well, well. No deaths at all.

18:00.690 --> 18:03.830
Elite hunters are not to be trifled with.

18:03.830 --> 18:08.620
All the monsters perished,
but so what? I can always make more.

18:10.120 --> 18:12.990
<i>There's no way to win if this keeps up.</i>

18:12.990 --> 18:16.040
<i>The one who has a chance to 
turn the tide of battle...</i>

18:16.610 --> 18:17.730
<i>is me.</i>

18:18.810 --> 18:23.470
Ahh, the Blessing of Might 
girl and her magic item.

18:23.470 --> 18:26.490
I'll be your opponent, if you can reach me.

18:26.490 --> 18:28.630
<i>Okay, it's now or never.</i>

18:30.650 --> 18:34.130
<i>The real me is far above 
the battlefield right now.</i>

18:34.130 --> 18:38.730
<i>Lammis flung me up here during the 
mayhem of that explosion spell.</i>

18:38.730 --> 18:42.970
<i>What she has on her back is a magic item 
Hulemy made, the "Housing-Only Me."</i>

18:43.300 --> 18:46.750
<i>The real me transformed, manipulated 
balloons using Telekinesis,</i>

18:46.750 --> 18:49.020
<i>and is directly above the Netherlord's head!</i>

18:49.020 --> 18:49.860
<i>Here goes!</i>

18:49.860 --> 18:52.580
<i>Form change!</i>

18:55.270 --> 18:58.960
<i>Japan's largest vending machine, which 
is placed at a certain fishing harbor!</i>

18:55.360 --> 19:05.120
<b>Ice</b>

18:58.960 --> 19:02.510
<i>It's been talked about on 
TV and is over 18 meters tall!</i>

19:02.510 --> 19:05.650
<i>Here it is, this ice vending machine!</i>

19:05.650 --> 19:07.800
Go on and struggle, hunters.

19:07.800 --> 19:10.630
Let's see if you can manage to reach—

19:11.750 --> 19:13.760
Wh-What is that?

19:13.760 --> 19:15.620
<i>A vending machine!</i>

19:25.150 --> 19:27.770
<i>I was ready in case I couldn't 
crush you right away!</i>

19:33.770 --> 19:36.030
<b>Automated External Defibrillator</b>

19:36.070 --> 19:37.280
<b>Release the lock and open this door</b>

19:36.450 --> 19:38.350
<i>Before I assumed this huge body,</i>

19:37.280 --> 19:38.360
<b>Coin Conversion</b>

19:37.280 --> 19:38.360
<b>Vending Compartment Shock Absorber</b>

19:37.280 --> 19:38.360
<b>Transformation</b>

19:37.280 --> 19:38.360
<b>Telekinesis</b>

19:37.280 --> 19:38.360
<b>Change Paint Color</b>

19:38.350 --> 19:42.150
<i>I switched back to the usual vending 
machine and prepared this!</i>

19:41.490 --> 19:42.490
<b>Use according to voice
 and visual instructions</b>

19:42.480 --> 19:44.120
<i>Thanks to me upping my physical strength,</i>

19:44.120 --> 19:47.370
<i>my maximum electroshock 
is now off the charts!</i>

19:47.370 --> 19:48.480
<i>Take this!</i>

20:07.320 --> 20:08.560
Boxxo!

20:08.790 --> 20:10.320
Are you okay?!

20:10.320 --> 20:11.240
Are you hurt?!

20:11.240 --> 20:12.910
No damage anywhere?!

20:11.950 --> 20:14.440
<i>I'm fine, Lammis. As you can see...</i>

20:15.310 --> 20:17.990
<i>Too bad. Too bad. Too bad.</i>

20:20.060 --> 20:22.060
<i>He's still alive!</i>

20:24.580 --> 20:27.070
This staff is precious, you see.

20:27.070 --> 20:28.830
I shall retrieve it.

20:28.830 --> 20:36.480
But still, you did manage to defeat what 
was merely my left arm transformed.

20:36.480 --> 20:38.460
That's worthy of praise.

20:38.460 --> 20:40.840
<i>His left arm? You gotta be kidding!</i>

20:41.110 --> 20:46.970
You defeated my offshoot, but I did 
still accomplish my original goal.

20:46.970 --> 20:48.840
Original goal?

20:50.180 --> 20:54.110
It was to gather all the 
capable hunters here.

20:54.340 --> 20:56.730
<i>Hulemy's hunch was right on!</i>

20:56.730 --> 21:01.480
If hunters or monster die 
inside this dungeon,

21:01.480 --> 21:06.740
the dungeon itself accumulates power 
proportional to the power of the dead.

21:06.740 --> 21:11.260
If I use that, I can produce 
more new monsters.

21:11.260 --> 21:14.250
That is the way this dungeon works.

21:14.470 --> 21:18.220
<i>I run on points. Is it 
something similar to that?</i>

21:18.790 --> 21:23.110
That's why it occurred to me to 
kill everything in this dungeon

21:23.110 --> 21:27.000
and produce a new pack of monsters.

21:27.000 --> 21:32.010
Now then, perhaps some of you have 
already figured out what I'm doing?

21:33.020 --> 21:37.000
Uh-oh. If all the aces are gathered here...

21:37.680 --> 21:40.370
the defense of the other 
strata is stretched thin.

21:40.370 --> 21:42.030
If they were to be attacked now...

21:42.030 --> 21:43.400
<i>It'd be the worst!</i>

21:43.590 --> 21:47.600
Now, don't you think you should hurry back?

21:47.600 --> 21:50.280
You can transfer to each stratum.

21:50.280 --> 21:54.220
But I'll see to it you can't 
go outside the dungeon.

21:54.220 --> 21:56.830
It's time to begin round two.

21:56.830 --> 22:02.600
Struggle hard and give your 
superb power to the dungeon.

23:35.050 --> 23:37.070
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Mutual Understanding</b>

23:37.970 --> 23:40.110
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
